«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSO Assyrian, the rod of mine anger, and the staff in their hand is mine indignation.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊI will send him against an hypocritical nation, and against the people of my wrath will I give him a charge, to take the spoil, and to take the prey, and to tread them down like the mire of the streets.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|Howbeit he meaneth not so, neither doth his heart think so; but it is in his heart to destroy and cut off nations not a few.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ2For he saith, Are not my princes altogether kings?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOIs not Calno as Carchemish? is not Hamath as Arpad? is not Samaria as Damascus?¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
