«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ×Wherefore it shall come to pass, that when the Lord hath performed his whole work upon mount Zion and on Jerusalem, I will punish the fruit of the stout heart of the king of Assyria, and the glory of his high looks.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙâFor he saith, By the strength of my hand I have done it, and by my wisdom; for I am prudent: and I have removed the bounds of the people, and have robbed their treasures, and I have put down the inhabitants like a valiant man:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊand my hand hath found as a nest the riches of the people: and as one gathereth eggs that are left, have I gathered all the earth; and there was none that moved the wing, or opened the mouth, or peeped.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙûShall the axe boast itself against him that heweth therewith? or shall the saw magnify itself against him that shaketh it? as if the rod should shake itself against them that lift it up, or as if the staff should lift up itself, as if it were no wood.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter
«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜Therefore shall the Lord, the Lord of hosts, send among his fat ones leanness; and under his glory he shall kindle a burning like the burning of a fire.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd the light of Israel shall be for a fire, and his Holy One for a flame: and it shall burn and devour his thorns and his briers in one day;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙand shall consume the glory of his forest, and of his fruitful field, both soul and body: and they shall be as when a standardbearer fainteth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRAnd the rest of the trees of his forest shall be few, that a child may write them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter
«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙäAnd it shall come to pass in that day, that the remnant of Israel, and such as are escaped of the house of Jacob, shall no more again stay upon him that smote them; but shall stay upon the LORD, the Holy One of Israel, in truth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIThe remnant shall return, even the remnant of Jacob, unto the mighty God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–For though thy people Israel be as the sand of the sea, yet a remnant of them shall return: the consumption decreed shall overflow with righteousness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbFor the Lord GOD of hosts shall make a consumption, even determined, in the midst of all the land.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter
«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÒTherefore thus saith the Lord GOD of hosts, O my people that dwellest in Zion, be not afraid of the Assyrian: he shall smite thee with a rod, and shall lift up his staff against thee, after the manner of Egypt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbFor yet a very little while, and the indignation shall cease, and mine anger in their destruction.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂAnd the LORD of hosts shall stir up a scourge for him according to the slaughter of Midian at the rock of Oreb: and as his rod was upon the sea, so shall he lift it up after the manner of Egypt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»And it shall come to pass in that day, that his burden shall be taken away from off thy shoulder, and his yoke from off thy neck, and the yoke shall be destroyed because of the anointing.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter
«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWHe is come to Aiath, he is passed to Migron; at Michmash he hath laid up his carriages:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrthey are gone over the passage: they have taken up their lodging at Geba; Ramah is afraid; Gibeah of Saul is fled.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZLift up thy voice, O daughter of Gallim: cause it to be heard unto Laish, O poor Anathoth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHMadmenah is removed; the inhabitants of Gebim gather themselves to flee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAs yet shall he remain at Nob that day: he shall shake his hand against the mount of the daughter of Zion, the hill of Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book§chapter
«first_verse!ªlast_verse"¦verses’„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜Behold, the Lord, the LORD of hosts, shall lop the bough with terror: and the high ones of stature shall be hewn down, and the haughty shall be humbled.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcAnd he shall cut down the thickets of the forest with iron, and Lebanon shall fall by a mighty one.¦layout ªlast_verse"